  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$ A composite number is a number that has more than two distinct factors.\n\nThe number $1$ is neither prime nor composite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the numbers in the list.\n\n- $40$ is *not* prime as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $10$ is a factor of $40:$ \n\n$$\n40=10\\times 4\n$$\n\n- $1$ is *not* prime since it has only one factor. Moreover, $1$ is *not* composite either.\n\n- $23$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $23.$\n\n- $36$ is *not* prime as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $6$ is a factor of $36:$ \n\n$$\n36=6\\times 6\n$$\n\n- $19$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $19.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$19$ and $23$ only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
